  "claims": [
    "A proof-pasting helper normalizes only proof-path association and units, and can paste one explicitly supplied Four cell into a consecutive segment. It emits ordinary Four constructor terms checked by the Lean kernel; it adds no generator or semantic equality oracle.",
    "Pathwise associator naturality in the first argument, its inverse corner, a middle-step square and a pentagon corner are derived in the retained pure Fin 31 presentation.",
    "The existing two distribution/projection diagrams, old pathwise beta naturality, categorical naturality and the pentagon derive a selector-suffix pasting rule from an actual projection square and an actual child square. No unconditional arbitrary whole-path generator is introduced.",
    "A two-case Side wrapper selects EXACTLY the frozen liftLeft or liftRight. mapLayout extends input references by Slot.left or Slot.right with the corresponding input ordering.",
    "For every arbitrary typed layout and every actual typed output Slot, the actual existing liftLeft/liftRight followed by the existing selectNormal on the extended layout is compared to association, prefixing the original selectNormal, and a zero-step endpoint correction. The comparison is recursively constructed on Slot.",
    "The endpoint correction comes only from the proved read_map equation and the definition of reifyRef on an embedded Slot. Its stepCount is exactly zero, proved using a general endpoint-transport count lemma.",
    "The arbitrary-layout theorem assumes neither injectivity nor surjectivity of routing. Repeated and unused input slots are allowed. It requires no supplied atomic higher witnesses and no new basic diagram family; the pure tag catalogue remains Fin 31.",
    "The existing MAC presentation embeds the arbitrary left/right comparison with empty support. The concrete example copies one MAC.before output, uses a repeated three-output layout, and selects the nested middle output.",
    "The sampled example retains exactly singleton stage support. Repaired joint-law equality in the updated checked model retains the correlated past, state and input; no independence of the copied sample is assumed."
  ],
  "finite_scope": {
    "unchanged_pure_schematic_tag_count": 31,
    "new_basic_generator_families": 0,
    "inputs": "Arbitrary Atom type, input/output/extra shapes, a typed Layout and a typed output Slot; both input-extension sides",
    "first_path": "Actual frozen liftLeft/liftRight track, postcomposed by the selector, then actual frozen selectNormal of the extended layout",
    "second_path": "An actual association step, prefixing the actual original selectNormal path, then an equality-transported identity from read_map",
    "correction_rewrite_leaves": 0,
    "pasting_helper": "Only association and units are automatic; inverse fragments are opaque and an actual Four witness is required for rewriting. The first matching consecutive segment is selected; this is not a complete proof search."
  },
  "limits": [
    "This proves lift/selection compatibility for all typed output positions. It does not yet establish substitution unit/associativity laws, higher idempotence of the full normalizer, or the unchanged actual canonical tensor square.",
    "The full eighteen-root and mixed rule catalogue still lacks a complete finite higher basis and arbitrary branching classifier.",
    "The zero count concerns only endpoint transport. Proof payload, layouts, contexts, higher constructors and checker time are not included. No fair total-cost compression advantage is proved.",
    "The helper program is not asserted to be a complete or performance-bounded solver. Each emitted proof used in the exported results is checked as an ordinary Lean proof term.",
    "The pure selector theorem does not discard conditional crypto requirements. The concrete MAC prefix retains and rechecks its stage condition.",
    "No new code-changing reduction, loss/time/resource bound or full continuing physical execution through oracle internals/keygen is supplied. Unregistered NativeConfiguredMAC integration remains excluded.",
    "Mathematical novelty remains unconfirmed. Categorical pasting and generic beta/eta coherence are not claimed as new abstract principles. No new external primary-source reading or independent review occurred."
  ],
  "next_obligations": [
    "Combine the actual identity projection squares with lift/selection compatibility to construct selection/substitution unit laws, including precise endpoint transports.",
    "Construct higher normalization idempotence and compare the unchanged actual canonical tensor normalization paths; then install the mixed tensor root contract.",
    "Keep the full original goal active: finite structural/mixed coverage, code-changing reductions/losses/resources, continuing oracle/keygen execution, fair shared-proof total costs and primary-source theorem-level novelty assessment."
  ],
